// Negative test: @extern without its parenthesized C signature string used to
// SIGSEGV the compiler (exit 139), not diagnose. The `extern` decorator branch
// in parser.sf ran `match (kind) { TkString(s) => s }` with no default arm on
// whatever token followed — here the `fun` keyword — and crashed.
//
// Expected: a parse error naming the required form, and a clean non-zero exit.
@extern fun my_abs(x: Float): Float

IO.println(my_abs(-3.0).to_string())
